        "description": "StarDist 2D model trained to identify the soma of migrating cortical interneurons, allowing for automated tracking of soma-based migration characteristics in confocal timelapse data. StarDist 2D model was trained on ground-truth annotated 1024x1024 images, with only the soma of mouse coritcal interneurons labelled. \n\nThe model can be used in combination with the script available here: https://github.com/hannahb94/Stardist/blob/main/Batch_stardist.ipynb  \n\nThe script allows for batch processing of 2D (Z-projected) timelapse data of migrating interneurons, automatically calculating velocity, nucleokinesis frequency and amplitude, polarity reversal frequency, average angle of polarity reversal, straightness index of migration track, and the percentage of time spent pausing.",
